    <!-- 2. Plate 02: steel coils -->
    <section class="plate" id="plate-coils" data-plate="02">
      <div class="plate__frame">
        <div class="plate__media">
          <video class="plate__video" data-video muted loop playsinline preload="none" poster="assets/photos/poster-02-coils.jpg" aria-hidden="true">
            <source data-src="assets/videos/02-coils.mp4" type="video/mp4">
          </video>
        </div>
        <div class="plate__shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="plate__copy">
          <h2 class="plate__pair">
          <span class="plate__word">Count.</span>
          <span class="plate__word plate__word--accent" data-accent="red">Measure.</span>
          <span class="plate__word">Record.</span>
          </h2>
          <div class="plate__story" data-reveal>
            <p>Steel does not forgive a vague report. Coils arrive with mill marks, strapping, edge protection and a weight on the packing list, and every one of those is a fact to be checked before the cargo moves again. A steel survey records count, condition, marks and any damage exactly as found, with photographs that match the tally. Pipe, plate and coil are surveyed the same way, at every hand-over, so the condition at each hand-over is on record.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="plate__meta">Steel coils in a covered store · AI-generated illustration based on a photograph from Nick’s files</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. Credentials -->
    <section class="section creds" id="credentials">
      <div class="section__inner">
        <h2 class="section__title">What the licenses certify</h2>
        <div class="creds__grid">
          <div class="creds__text">
            <dl class="facts">
              <div class="facts__row" data-reveal>
                <dt class="facts__term">Second Mate Unlimited</dt>
                <dd class="facts__desc">
                  <p>A U.S. merchant mariner deck officer license in the unlimited-tonnage class. What it covers in practice depends on the routes, endorsements and limitations printed on the credential.</p>
                  <p>Why it matters to you: a stowage plan, a stability calculation or a lashing arrangement is read the way a watch officer reads it, not only the way an inspector does.</p>
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div class="facts__row" data-reveal>
                <dt class="facts__term">1600-Ton Master</dt>
                <dd class="facts__desc">
                  <p>A merchant mariner master’s license in the 1600 gross ton class, likewise subject to the routes, endorsements and limitations on the credential.</p>
                  <p>Why it matters to you: it brings a master’s frame of reference, navigation, stability and vessel safety, to a towing survey or a loading survey.</p>
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div class="facts__row" data-reveal>
                <dt class="facts__term">Surveying</dt>
                <dd class="facts__desc">
                  <p>About ten years surveying. Previously employed at EIMC.</p>
                </dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
            <p class="creds__note" data-reveal>Credentials as supplied by Nick Salazar; not independently verified on this page.</p>
          </div>
          <figure class="creds__figure" data-reveal>
            <img class="creds__img" src="assets/photos/hero.jpg" width="1920" height="1440" loading="lazy" alt="A large grey finned unit with yellow circular plates suspended from a ship’s crane on a long spreader beam, with shipping containers on deck below and a bright, partly cloudy sky.">
            <figcaption class="creds__caption">A heavy unit lifted on a spreader beam. From Nick’s files.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. Plate 03: crawler crane -->
    <section class="plate" id="plate-crane" data-plate="03">
      <div class="plate__frame">
        <div class="plate__media">
          <video class="plate__video" data-video muted loop playsinline preload="none" poster="assets/photos/poster-03-crane.jpg" aria-hidden="true">
            <source data-src="assets/videos/03-crane.mp4" type="video/mp4">
          </video>
        </div>
        <div class="plate__shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="plate__copy">
          <h2 class="plate__pair">
          <span class="plate__word">Rig.</span>
          <span class="plate__word plate__word--accent">Lift.</span>
          <span class="plate__word">Land.</span>
          </h2>
          <div class="plate__story" data-reveal>
            <p>A heavy lift is planned on paper and proven in the air. Rigging, sling angles, the crane’s set-up, the receiving railcar or deck, and the tie-down that follows are each checked against the plan before and after the load leaves the ground. Nick attends heavy lift and project cargo operations and railcar loadings as an independent surveyor, and reports what was done, not what was intended.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="plate__meta">Crawler crane lifting a unit onto a railcar · AI-generated illustration based on a photograph from Nick’s files</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 5. Services -->
    <section class="section services" id="services">
      <div class="section__inner">
        <h2 class="section__title">Services</h2>
        <p class="section__lede" data-reveal>Every survey type Nick offers, and what you get from each one.</p>
        <ul class="services__list">
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">Break bulk</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">Condition, count and securing of non-containerized cargo, recorded at loading or discharge.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">Heavy lift / project cargo</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">Attendance at lifts and moves of oversized units, checked against the rigging and stowage plan.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">Steel pipe / plate / coils</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">Tally, marks and condition of steel at each hand-over, with damage noted as found.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">Stock throughput warehouse inspections</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">Inspection of stored inventory and the facility holding it, for stock insured across storage and transit.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">Cargo claim surveys</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">The nature, apparent cause and extent of loss or damage, as observed on attendance and recorded for the claim file.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">CSC container inspections</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">Structural inspection of containers against the requirements of the International Convention for Safe Containers.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">Draft survey</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">Cargo quantity determined from the vessel’s drafts and displacement, at loading and at discharge.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">Towing survey</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">Inspection of the tow, the towing gear and the connections before the voyage begins.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">Loading / stowage surveys</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">Verification that cargo is stowed, blocked and lashed as planned, before the hold or the doors close.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">Railcar loading</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">Loading and securement of cargo on railcars, documented at the ramp.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">Truck loading</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">Loading and securement on trailers, documented before the truck leaves the yard.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">Jack and slide</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">Attendance at hydraulic jacking and skidding moves of heavy, tip-sensitive equipment.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">Airfreight</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">Condition and packing of air cargo, surveyed before build-up.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="services__item" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="services__name">Packing / crate surveys</h3>
          <p class="services__desc">Export packing and crating checked against the cargo and the route, before closure.</p>
        </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 6. Plate 04: cargo braced in a container -->
    <section class="plate" id="plate-drums" data-plate="04">
      <div class="plate__frame">
        <div class="plate__media">
          <video class="plate__video" data-video muted loop playsinline preload="none" poster="assets/photos/poster-04-drums.jpg" aria-hidden="true">
            <source data-src="assets/videos/04-drums.mp4" type="video/mp4">
          </video>
        </div>
        <div class="plate__shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="plate__copy">
          <h2 class="plate__pair">
          <span class="plate__word">Block.</span>
          <span class="plate__word plate__word--accent" data-accent="yellow">Brace.</span>
          <span class="plate__word">Lash.</span>
          </h2>
          <div class="plate__story" data-reveal>
            <p>Inside a container the cargo has nowhere to go but into the walls. Timber blocking, bracing frames and lashings have to hold through road, rail and sea, and how they are fitted is the whole difference between cargo that arrives and cargo that shifts. A loading and stowage survey documents the securing as fitted, with the container number, the seal and photographs, before the doors close.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="plate__meta">Cylindrical units braced inside a container · AI-generated illustration based on a photograph from Nick’s files</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

