    <!-- 8. Plate 05: tarped loads on flat racks -->
    <section class="plate" id="plate-containers" data-plate="05">
      <div class="plate__frame">
        <div class="plate__media">
          <video class="plate__video" data-video muted loop playsinline preload="none" poster="assets/photos/poster-05-containers.jpg" aria-hidden="true">
            <source data-src="assets/videos/05-containers.mp4" type="video/mp4">
          </video>
        </div>
        <div class="plate__shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="plate__copy">
          <h2 class="plate__pair">
          <span class="plate__word">Wrap.</span>
          <span class="plate__word plate__word--accent" data-accent="sky">Secure.</span>
          <span class="plate__word">Ship.</span>
          </h2>
          <div class="plate__story" data-reveal>
            <p>Break bulk cargo travels exposed: flat racks, trailers, deck stow, weather. Tarps, nets and straps only do their work if they are fitted and tensioned correctly, and only matter if the cargo beneath them was sound when it was covered. Nick surveys break bulk and truck loadings for condition, marks and securing, and produces a record the receiving end can be measured against.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="plate__meta">Tarped loads on flat racks in a yard · AI-generated illustration based on a photograph from Nick’s files</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 9. Plate 06: crate -->
    <section class="plate" id="plate-warehouse" data-plate="06">
      <div class="plate__frame">
        <div class="plate__media">
          <video class="plate__video" data-video muted loop playsinline preload="none" poster="assets/photos/poster-06-warehouse.jpg" aria-hidden="true">
            <source data-src="assets/videos/06-warehouse.mp4" type="video/mp4">
          </video>
        </div>
        <div class="plate__shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="plate__copy">
          <h2 class="plate__pair">
          <span class="plate__word">Pack.</span>
          <span class="plate__word plate__word--accent" data-accent="sky">Protect.</span>
          <span class="plate__word">Prove.</span>
          </h2>
          <div class="plate__story" data-reveal>
            <p>Packing problems show up long after the crate is closed, when it is too late to fix them. A packing and crate survey checks the crate, the cradle, the bracing, the wrapping and the marks against what the cargo needs for the route ahead, and photographs the work before it is closed up. If the crate is right, the report says so. If it is not, the report says that too, while there is still time to correct it.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="plate__meta">Wrapped machine in an open timber crate · AI-generated illustration based on a photograph from Nick’s files</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 10. Plate 07: roller dolly -->
    <section class="plate" id="plate-yard" data-plate="07">
      <div class="plate__frame">
        <div class="plate__media">
          <video class="plate__video" data-video muted loop playsinline preload="none" poster="assets/photos/poster-07-yard.jpg" aria-hidden="true">
            <source data-src="assets/videos/07-yard.mp4" type="video/mp4">
          </video>
        </div>
        <div class="plate__shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="plate__copy">
          <h2 class="plate__pair">
          <span class="plate__word">Weigh.</span>
          <span class="plate__word">Watch.</span>
          <span class="plate__word plate__word--accent" data-accent="yellow">Witness.</span>
          </h2>
          <div class="plate__story" data-reveal>
            <p>Airfreight moves fast and leaves a short paper trail. High-value, time-critical cargo still needs someone to confirm its condition, its packing and its securing on the pallet or dolly before it is built up and gone. Nick surveys airfreight shipments with the same discipline as an ocean lift: condition as found, photographs, and a report written for the shipper and the underwriter alike.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="plate__meta">Units on a roller dolly in a cargo warehouse · AI-generated illustration based on a photograph from Nick’s files</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 11. Why independent -->
    <section class="section why" id="why">
      <div class="section__inner">
        <h2 class="section__title">Why an independent surveyor</h2>
        <div class="why__points">
          <article class="why__point" data-reveal>
            <h3 class="why__heading">No side to take</h3>
            <p class="why__text">Nick is engaged by one party and answerable to the facts. That independence is what makes a survey report worth relying on by everyone who has to read it.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="why__point" data-reveal>
            <h3 class="why__heading">Evidence built to be read later</h3>
            <p class="why__text">Photographs, tallies, measurements and a clear timeline, written for someone who was not there and needs to understand what happened months afterwards.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="why__point" data-reveal>
            <h3 class="why__heading">One name on the report</h3>
            <p class="why__text">The person who attends is the person who writes and signs. Questions about the survey go to the surveyor who was on site.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 12. Contact: assignment brief -->
    <!-- PRE-PUBLICATION DEPENDENCY: contact destination (phone/email) not supplied; wire before publishing -->
    <section class="section brief" id="contact">
      <div class="section__inner">
        <h2 class="section__title">Build an assignment brief</h2>
        <p class="section__lede" data-reveal>There is no form to submit here. Describe the assignment and this page assembles a plain-text brief you can copy or download, then send through whatever channel you already use.</p>
        <form class="brief__form" id="brief-form" novalidate>
          <div class="field">
            <label class="field__label" for="bf-service">Survey type</label>
            <select class="input" id="bf-service" name="service" aria-describedby="bf-service-help">
              <option value="">Choose a survey type</option>
                <option value="Break bulk">Break bulk</option>
                <option value="Heavy lift / project cargo">Heavy lift / project cargo</option>
                <option value="Steel pipe / plate / coils">Steel pipe / plate / coils</option>
                <option value="Stock throughput warehouse inspection">Stock throughput warehouse inspection</option>
                <option value="Cargo claim survey">Cargo claim survey</option>
                <option value="CSC container inspection">CSC container inspection</option>
                <option value="Draft survey">Draft survey</option>
                <option value="Towing survey">Towing survey</option>
                <option value="Loading / stowage survey">Loading / stowage survey</option>
                <option value="Railcar loading">Railcar loading</option>
                <option value="Truck loading">Truck loading</option>
                <option value="Jack and slide">Jack and slide</option>
                <option value="Airfreight">Airfreight</option>
                <option value="Packing / crate survey">Packing / crate survey</option>
            </select>
            <p class="field__help" id="bf-service-help"></p>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label class="field__label" for="bf-cargo">Cargo description</label>
            <textarea class="input input--area" id="bf-cargo" name="cargo" rows="3" aria-describedby="bf-cargo-help"></textarea>
            <p class="field__help" id="bf-cargo-help"></p>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label class="field__label" for="bf-where">Port or facility</label>
            <input class="input" id="bf-where" name="where" type="text" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="bf-where-help">
            <p class="field__help" id="bf-where-help"></p>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label class="field__label" for="bf-when">Timing</label>
            <input class="input" id="bf-when" name="when" type="text" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="bf-when-help">
            <p class="field__help" id="bf-when-help"></p>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label class="field__label" for="bf-evidence">Evidence you need</label>
            <textarea class="input input--area" id="bf-evidence" name="evidence" rows="3" aria-describedby="bf-evidence-help"></textarea>
            <p class="field__help" id="bf-evidence-help"></p>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label class="field__label" for="bf-name">Your name</label>
            <input class="input" id="bf-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" aria-describedby="bf-name-help">
            <p class="field__help" id="bf-name-help"></p>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label class="field__label" for="bf-org">Organisation</label>
            <input class="input" id="bf-org" name="org" type="text" autocomplete="organization" aria-describedby="bf-org-help">
            <p class="field__help" id="bf-org-help"></p>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label class="field__label" for="bf-contact">How to reach you</label>
            <input class="input" id="bf-contact" name="contact" type="text" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="bf-contact-help">
            <p class="field__help" id="bf-contact-help"></p>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label class="field__label" for="bf-notes">Anything else</label>
            <textarea class="input input--area" id="bf-notes" name="notes" rows="3" aria-describedby="bf-notes-help"></textarea>
            <p class="field__help" id="bf-notes-help"></p>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <span class="field__label">Assignment brief</span>
            <pre class="brief__output" id="brief-output" tabindex="0"></pre>
          </div>
          <div class="brief__actions">
            <button type="button" class="btn btn--fill" id="brief-copy">Copy brief</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn--outline" id="brief-download">Download .txt</button>
          </div>
          <p class="brief__status" id="brief-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
          <p class="brief__note">Nothing is sent from this page. Copy or download the brief and send it through your own channel.</p>
        </form>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <footer class="foot" id="foot">
    <p class="foot__line">Watch the cargo. Write it down. Stand behind it.</p>
    <div class="foot__meta">
      <span class="foot__mark">Nick Salazar</span>
      <span class="foot__muted">Credentials as supplied by Nick Salazar. Video plates are AI-generated illustrations based on photographs from Nick’s files; gallery photographs are the originals.</span>
      <span class="foot__muted">© 2026 Nick Salazar</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script type="module" src="app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>


